# No version or release date here, so this file can't fall behind a release: cite the version you
# used (`immunum --version`, `immunum.__version__`) alongside it.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use immunum in your research, please cite it as below, with the version you used."
type: software
title: "immunum: antibody and T-cell receptor sequence numbering"
abstract: >-
  Fast antibody and T-cell receptor variable domain numbering (IMGT, Kabat, Chothia, Martin, AHo)
  and FR/CDR segmentation, by semi-global alignment against position-specific scoring matrices
  built from consensus sequences. Available as a Rust crate and command-line tool, a Python
  package with a Polars plugin, and an npm package.
authors:
  - name: ENPICOM
    email: dev@enpicom.com
    website: "https://www.enpicom.com"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ENPICOM/immunum"
url: "https://immunum.enpicom.com"
keywords:
  - antibody
  - T-cell receptor
  - numbering
  - IMGT
  - Kabat
  - Chothia
  - bioinformatics
